@page "/"

<PageTitle>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor · Web App sample</PageTitle>

<h1>Jenin.FontAwesome.Blazor · Blazor Web App sample</h1>

<p>
    This sample hosts the same Font Awesome components under every hosting model a Blazor Web App
    offers: static server-side rendering, Interactive Server, Interactive WebAssembly, and
    Interactive Auto. The render mode is the only thing that changes; the component markup does not.
</p>

<p>Pick a page to see the library behave the same way on each host:</p>

<ul>
    <li><a href="static-ssr">Static SSR</a>: HTML is rendered on the server with no interactivity.</li>
    <li><a href="interactive-server">Interactive Server</a>: interactivity over a SignalR circuit, prerendered.</li>
    <li><a href="interactive-server-no-prerender">Interactive Server (no prerender)</a>: the same circuit without prerendering.</li>
    <li><a href="interactive-webassembly">Interactive WebAssembly</a>: interactivity runs in the browser.</li>
    <li><a href="interactive-auto">Interactive Auto</a>: server first, then WebAssembly once downloaded.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    A meaningful icon renders on this static page without any interactivity:
    <Icon IconStyle=IconStyle.Solid IconName="fa-house" Title="Home" Decorative=false />
</p>
